      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The algorithm constructs a constant-size anchor-pair candidate set, builds a linear-time constant approximation and an O(1/epsilon^2) certificate, and reduces the general problem to O(1/epsilon) candidate slab orientations. Its fixed-orientation subroutine maintains constrained convex-hull widths under sliding-window updates, with amortized tangent/antipodal searches and exact optimization. All original appendix proofs, including the 10-approximation, optimization, lower-bound and zero-width cases, are included. The linked algorithm suite and its certificate/support results are counted together.",
